d sells apparels and related accessories for men, women, and children in the United States and internationally. The company offers jeans, casual and dress pants, activewears, tops, shorts, skirts, dresses, jumpsuits, shirts, sweaters, jackets, footwear, and related accessories under the Levi's, Levi Strauss Signature, Denizen, and Beyond Yoga brands. It sells its products through third-party retailers, such as department stores, specialty retailers, third-party e-commerce sites, and franchisees; and directly to consumers through company-operated mainline and outlet stores, company-operated e-commerce sites, and select shop-in-shops located in department stores and other third-party retail locations. The company also operates brand-dedicated stores and shop-in-shops. Levi Strauss & Co. was founded in 1853 and is headquartered in San Francisco, California.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Michelle D. Gass | CEO, President & Director | Age 57 | Compensation: $4.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 19K people. Revenue per employee of $331K ranks in the below the sector median among Consumer Cyclical peers. Each employee generates $16K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 15\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Levi Strauss & Co is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $9.3B market cap on $6.3B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +1% over the past three years and +3% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 23% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 13-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat. Gross margins of 53% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $308M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 5 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, with adequate 0.92\u00d7 cash conversion.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.2\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 14\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield of 2.6% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 2.5% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 80% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.8020098190955135},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (11.1% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Heavy insider selling (net $23.8M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-23809961.69},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 12% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Levi's: Driving Supply Chain Decarbonization","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/energy/articles/levis-driving-supply-chain-decarbonization-143000361.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794580200.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.361,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Levi Strauss & Co. (NYSE:LEVI) and lululemon athletica (NASDAQ:LULU) Head to Head Analysis","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/levi-strauss-co-nyselevi-and-lululemon-athletica-nasdaqlulu-head-to-head-analysis.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794578333.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.934,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Does New Sustainability Chief Change The Bull Case For Levi Strauss (LEVI)?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/consumer-durables/nyse-levi/levi-strauss/news/does-new-sustainability-chief-change-the-bull-case-for-levi","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794562044.897,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.361,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Avoiding Lag: Real-Time Signals in (LEVI) Movement","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/151/Avoiding_Lag:_Real-Time_Signals_in_LEVI_Movement_111226083201_1794490321.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794490321.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.823,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Levi Strauss (LEVI) Could Be 29% Overvalued After Sustainability Hire And Early Black Friday Sale","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/consumer-durables/nyse-levi/levi-strauss/news/levi-strauss-levi-could-be-29-overvalued-after-sustainabilit","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794471825.746,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.84,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Levi Strauss (LEVI) Stock Looks Cheap Relative To Its Earnings","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simpl